      "notes": "Invictvs is set in the gladiatorial arenas, and the following mature content appears throughout the game.\r\n\r\nViolence. Every match is armed combat fought to the finish with swords, tridents and nets. Opponents are defeated by reducing their health to zero, and a defeated opponent delivers a dying line of dialogue before the match ends. Bleeding is a core combat mechanic: blood spray, blood mist and pools of blood on the sand are drawn as visual effects during fights. The art style is stylized hand-painted pixel art. There is no dismemberment, no open wounds and no photorealistic gore.\r\n\r\nDeath of the player character. When the player is finally defeated, their owner turns his thumb down and the player character is put to death by the sword. The scene is presented as narration over a still illustration of an empty arena \u2014 a fallen helmet and a sword planted in the sand. The killing itself is never shown.\r\n\r\nSlavery and human trafficking. The player character is an enslaved gladiator who is owned, trained and made to fight for his owner's profit. The prologue depicts his village being burned and his family being killed, and then depicts him being sold at a slave auction where buyers handle his body and force his mouth open to inspect him. Winning his freedom from his owner is the goal of the game.\r\n\r\nAlcohol. Optional events between matches include drinking at a tavern and sharing stolen wine. No drug use is depicted.\r\n\r\nThe game contains no sexual content, no nudity, no depictions of sexual assault or\r\nnon-consensual sex, and no depictions of suicide or self-harm."
